{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "lanes_forcing_contraction",
    "description": "A pointwise operator on a 6 x 5 x 4 grid fed by forcing data the way a regridded emission inventory is. F and G are data-fed array parameters (forcing slots); the source is never read, so the default forcing set holds their declared defaults. E over 30 target cells is a whole-domain contraction of the forcing array F over 40 source cells (it reads forcing only: no state, no t), Exy over (lon, lat) reads E at the computed flattened subscript (j-1)*6+i, and the right-hand side also reads the forcing arrays G at the non-affine subscript floor((i+2j)/2) and F at the affine subscript (j-1)*6+i+5, which a lane program pre-gathers per lane. A lane program evaluates E once per forcing set, not once per call or per chunk of lanes.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciAST test suite"
    ],
    "created": "2026-11-26T00:00:00Z",
    "tags": [
      "conformance",
      "range_restricted_rhs"
    ]
  },
